  "body": "**Link to problem area**: https://spec.matrix.org/v1.8/client-server-api/#get_matrixclientversions and https://spec.matrix.org/v1.8/#specification-versions\r\n\r\n**Issue**\r\nThere seem to be at least 2 if not 3 different interpretations on this. Js-Sdk thinks that implementing 1.8 also requires implementation of 1.1. But from a new implementor perspective, it feels odd to implement all versions from 1.1 until 1.8. It not only slows down the implementation but also makes it at least 4x as hard.\r\n\r\nThis is a little different than room versions which exist in parallel. Also I am aware that obviously there will be an overlap on the update periods since sdks have to catch up. However it feels odd to needing to implement almost over 2 years of specifications for a server to work.\r\n\r\nThe relevant js-sdk issue is at https://github.com/matrix-org/matrix-js-sdk/issues/3915 (There is some more info but to avoid unnecessary duplication I won't copy that over here)\r\n",
